* = budget-free row (mean stores 1 vector; maha stores a full DxD covariance,
    ~2300x the R=256 budget) -- printed once, not swept.
P1 cal is the honest dataset-ID number: raw argmax rewards whichever dataset happens
    to have the tightest descriptor, so scores are z-normalised on held-out own-train.
A cone win counts ONLY if it holds at matched R, over `subspace` (= same score without
    non-negativity), and in the frozen space (= no per-dataset LoRA fingerprint).
